From 0c30b92a50983a5c3c6a0452593af813b681a5db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Spindler <richard@lateralblast.com.au>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:20:19 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] aes-ctr-mt: make the same changes in the non-OpenSSL 3
 implementation

cipher-ctr-mt.c is the multithreaded AES-CTR cipher for builds without
OpenSSL 3. It had the same defects as cipher-ctr-mt-functions.c: the shared
evp_ptrs hash with its race, 4-byte key and unchecked lookup, the global
thread and queue counts, the pointer to the caller's key, an exit(1) from a
pregen thread on an invalid key length, and an unchecked malloc and
EVP_CIPHER_CTX_new. Make the same change there.

This file is only built without OpenSSL 3. It compiles with no warnings
when built that way, but it has not been run.

Changelog: sphynx 0.0.4, 0.0.5, 0.0.6, 0.0.8, 0.0.9, 0.1.0

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
